mods: dev-sandbox, fw-3d
timeout: 120s
hide: false
# 3D phase M1 (docs/possible_3d_work.md): the probe cube. Launch it with MEWFW_MESH_PROBE=1 (tile 3,3) or
# MEWFW_MESH_PROBE=<col>,<row> in the environment — `npm run test:artprobe -- --mesh` sets it — and mewframework draws a
# flat magenta unit cube (0.8 tiles) on that tile through a draw functor submitted after the world camera's units
# layer, depth-tested against the main RT. It logs "mesh probe f=.. tile=(c,r) ndc=(x y z) canvas=(x y)" (the
# projected tile centre) and "mesh draw ..." (the GL state it found, its GL errors) into mod_logs/mewframework.log;
# editor/src/core/art/mesh-measure.ts reads those lines and the shots (a magenta patch at the projected centre; refuses
# when the shots are byte-identical). Without the variable nothing is drawn and this is a plain fight with shots.
# M2 textures: MEWFW_MESH_PROBE_TEXTURE=<name under textures/> and MEWFW_MESH_PROBE_PALETTE=<palette.png row> set the probe
# model's material (default: textures/models/<stem>.png when present, palette off); the "mesh object ... ndc=.. tex=..
# palette=.." lines + mesh-measure.ts judgeColourPatch measure the drawn colours around the model's anchor.
# The spawned Rat gives the sprites/mesh occlusion record (phase M2 is not done: the cube is drawn over its layer).
wait frames 120
seed 42
enter TacticsTest
wait frames 60
cmd spawn Rat
expect console "Spawned Rat" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "mesh-a"
wait frames 45
shot "mesh-b"
wait frames 30
quit
